{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies","id":1546723,"title":"\"Do-While\" and \"Do-Until\" Spell Contingencies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-07T07:15:05-08:00","id":1546723,"title":"\"Do-While\" and \"Do-Until\" Spell Contingencies","content":"A Virtual Adept character, of the reality hacker variety, has started looking into effect contingencies not involving hanging effects. Players in the games I run are considerate enough to let me work out the details of novel awakened magickal applications between sessions, by letting me know that their character is &quot;working on&quot; some approach which the written materials don't provide clear immediate examples of. This has worked out well.<br /> <br /> What he is wanting to do is use Entropy conjunctionally to provide a condition under which an active effect will <i>cancel</i> itself, similar to a hanging effect which goes off at some future point based on certain conditions. As an example, the mage works an effect which provides power to a lightbulb, with the condition that the effect expires if someone walks through the doorway of the room it's lighting, provided that the duration of the effect doesn't expire naturally first.<br /> <br /> So far as I can tell based on the available M20 material, this sort of thing would simply require a conjunctional Entropy effect of an appropriate level relative to the contingency. Time wouldn't seem to be necessary, as the effect isn't a hanging one being &quot;cast into the future.&quot; (I'm basing this mostly on what's presented about this in How Do You DO That.)<br /> <br /> Does anyone know of a written example of this, which I might have missed somewhere? We tend NOT to do house rules unless the existing ones outright don't cover some potential situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T08:11:33-08:00","id":1546727,"title":"","content":"I can't remember of any example like that, but I'm not sure you need Entropy. I mean, for you lightbulb example, I'd say all you need is Forces+Prime (to light the bulb) and Life, to scan for people entering the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T08:41:15-08:00","id":1546729,"title":"","content":"All you need is Entropy 2. Besides the desired effect of course.<br /> <br /> Entropy 2 is the &quot;conditional&quot; for any sort of effects. So, while trying to build you &quot;else if&quot; algorithm, you just add Entropy 2 to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T10:08:36-08:00","id":1546731,"title":"","content":"HDYDT suggests it would be Entropy 4. I personally use Entropy 3 but i modified the spheres in my games.<br /> Also it could be tied to Correspondence as described in the ward section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 12-07-2024, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T10:36:52-08:00","id":1546733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546727#post1546727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember of any example like that, but I'm not sure you need Entropy. I mean, for you lightbulb example, I'd say all you need is Forces+Prime (to light the bulb) and Life, to scan for people entering the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that this is largely guesswork and interpretation on my part, since it's not spelled out anywhere I can locate, Entropy <i>seems</i> to work conjunctionally to create &quot;conditions&quot; in other effects by deliberately creating a sort of &quot;loose thread&quot; in the weave of an overall working, and ties that to some other potential condition in the tapestry, deterministically linking the two. I can imagine an Etherite describing this as some sort of &quot;causal ethric entanglement.&quot; The mage who's trying to do this thinks of this application of Entropy as coding conditions (if-then, do-while, do-until, etc.) and function breaks. The player actually works out his rotes in the form of pseudocode on paper, he's that much into the &quot;reality hacking&quot; business.<br /> <br /> In the case of hanging effects with conditions, the &quot;loose thread&quot; is the Time aspect. When some other specified condition causes it to be pulled, that undoes the temporal statis the rest of the working has been locked into.<br /> <br /> The most complete explanation in the written material I can find requires different levels of Entropy, depending on what you're wanting to link an effect to conditionally. The levels seem to be based on what sorts of things Entropy itself can work with in a probabilistic sense. (I am not totally clear on what counts as &quot;ideas,&quot; requiring Entropy 5, except maybe a condition based on some person or group of people merely thinking of something?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-07-2024, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T10:48:32-08:00","id":1546734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546731#post1546731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HDYDT suggests it would be Entropy 4. I personally use Entropy 3 but i modified the spheres in my games.<br /> Also it could be tied to Correspondence as described in the ward section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy 3 for objects and events, 4 for anything directly to do with living things, and 5 for &quot;ideas.&quot; In the case of specific objects or living things, this might be more difficult to apply without some familiarity with that particular subject, but that's not explicitly stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","user":"Steve Bridger","date":". 12-07-2024, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-07T16:31:18-08:00","id":1546751,"title":"","content":"Pre-M20: Entropy 2, maybe an appropriate sensory Sphere at 1 (less common in the books, but sometimes included/suggested).<br /> M20: Variable level of Entropy at ST discretion as largely been discussed already. Though Entropy 2 + Sensory Sphere 1 would still be a viable alternative to higher Entropy for different types of Patterns.<br /> <br /> The more complex the set of conditions desired, the more appealing the Correspondence route gets, since you can use the designated area as matrix to key different conditions off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-08T21:19:25-08:00","id":1546788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546731#post1546731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HDYDT suggests it would be Entropy 4. I personally use Entropy 3 but i modified the spheres in my games.<br /> Also it could be tied to Correspondence as described in the ward section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but HDYDT is utter garbage.<br /> <br /> In every single edition, this has always been Entropy 2. It also fits the level description, while it doesn't fit the lvl description of Entropy 4 (or 3) not even one bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T05:21:38-08:00","id":1546792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546788#post1546788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but HDYDT is utter garbage.<br /> <br /> In every single edition, this has always been Entropy 2. It also fits the level description, while it doesn't fit the lvl description of Entropy 4 (or 3) not even one bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah its not great but if we look only by the main rulebook its time 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T06:54:52-08:00","id":1546793,"title":"","content":"What Time 4 does, specifically, is put a spell in suspended animation until a trigger point is reached. I would argue that seems like overkill for &quot;Do While&quot; or Do Until&quot; although I suppose it could work if only the cancel clause is suspended.<br /> <br /> M20, unfortunately, is missing clear rules for making spells able to detect changing conditions, so it gives a different answer every time it comes up. Time triggers don't need extra spheres, wards use associated spheres at the highest level they can be inflated to. The former acts like any spell can detect changing conditions without extra spheres. The latter acts like detection takes the same skill as transmutation. <br /> <br /> I don't think either makes sense, though if I had to choose between the two I would go with no additional spheres on the grounds of usability. My recommendation, though, is that any time a spell needs to detect something (or touch something without making changes) use [Appropriate Sphere] 2. Entropy 2 would work for most &quot;event&quot; triggers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T08:53:34-08:00","id":1546797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546793#post1546793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Time 4 does, specifically, is put a spell in suspended animation until a trigger point is reached. I would argue that seems like overkill for &quot;Do While&quot; or Do Until&quot; although I suppose it could work if only the cancel clause is suspended.<br /> <br /> M20, unfortunately, is missing clear rules for making spells able to detect changing conditions, so it gives a different answer every time it comes up. Time triggers don't need extra spheres, wards use associated spheres at the highest level they can be inflated to. The former acts like any spell can detect changing conditions without extra spheres. The latter acts like detection takes the same skill as transmutation.<br /> <br /> I don't think either makes sense, though if I had to choose between the two I would go with no additional spheres on the grounds of usability. My recommendation, though, is that any time a spell needs to detect something (or touch something without making changes) use [Appropriate Sphere] 2. Entropy 2 would work for most &quot;event&quot; triggers.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, officially the requirement has always been Time 4 Entropy 2, which I fully agree is absolutely overkill, and I also say that it doesn't make sense given what it is supposed to do. I didn't include Time 4 because I thought that was already simplicity, but I houserule it out and make it Entropy 2 alone.<br /> <br /> The reason for the usage of Time 4, as explained in official sources from 1st ed to rev is that it is used to &quot;hold the spell&quot;, as if you need to keep the spell frozen in time.<br /> <br /> That... Makes no sense thou. Because it is Entropy 2 that do all the job. Entropy 2 is used to cause the spell to &quot;selective fail&quot;. For instance, the ward spell will let any redheads go through; this means that the ward will always be working, except when a redhead goes through, upon which Entropy 2 will cause it to selective fail.<br /> <br /> Time 4 doesn't do anything really, and this is yet another instance upon which the writers &quot;go with their feelings&quot;, as they so often do, instead of what the levels of the Spheres were supposed to do. In fact, adding Time 4 is less than useless, because it means that Entropy 2 will be causing the Time 4 effect of &quot;holding the spell paralyzed in Time&quot; to selectively fail or not, instead of the main spell itself, which is stupid.<br /> <br /> I also disagree on the usage of other Spheres. Entropy 2 is all that you need. You don't need Matter to identify someone carrying a firearm, or Life to identify a redhead, which would be the targets of your ward for example. All you need is Entropy because you're identifying DESTINY. &quot;This ward is <b>DESTINED</b> to ignite upon redheads&quot;. It doesn't matter if the effect can make a chemical analysis of the person's body hairs.<br /> <br /> It's just like using Entropy to shoot 2 arrows and to hit the 2 people at the end in a line of 3 but not the person at front. You don't need Life to do that, because you're dealing with Fate, Destiny, Probability. Likewise, conditional spells need Entropy 2 (and according to RAW Time 4, but I hope Ive already made a good case to why this is stupid and should be removed), because you don't need the spell to analyze the subject, you just need the Fate or Destiny conditions to be set. Therefore, no other Spheres are required - except for whatever Spheres are required for the underlined effect itself.<br /> <br /> For example: <b>Bullet Time</b> - Time 3, Entropy 2. Whenever someone shoots at you, you gain increased speed.<br /> <br /> Time 3 accelerates time (as per the rules, one extra action per turn for every 2 successes), while Entropy 2 is the &quot;trigger&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, the thing about Triggers is that you have to spend successes on duration. Now, for the above Bullet Time Routine above for instance, I would say that keeping that for less than a day would be useless. Now, you can of course just simply constantly walk around with a bunch of triggers spells permanently attached; just remember to enforce the increased difficulty rules for simultaneous spells being held on but hey, on many occasions I would trade the capability to launch new spells (due to prohibitive dif) for having a ton of cool powers &quot;always on&quot; on me at all times (like for instance instant regeneration all the time, mental shields, the &quot;All Seeing Eye&quot; effect which I laid in another topic that has all the lvl 1 and some lvl 2 Spheres to basically give you Spider Man's &quot;spider senses&quot; on steroids, &quot;Perfect Escape&quot; which I'm just inventing right now - Corr 3 Entropy 2, which causes you to teleport to a safe location whenever you're in mortal danger and a few others. Walking around with a bunch of permanent effects may be better than being able to cast spells at will - and remember, you can truly have a ton of them)<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T09:10:42-08:00","id":1546801,"title":"","content":"To make sure I understand you correctly: <br /> <br /> There are two ways I could see constructing a Bullet Time spell that turns on when someone shoots at you. The obvious one from looking at the rules is a Bullet Time spell put in suspended animation with an event trigger. This would be Time 4 for Trigger Effect (plus Entropy 2 if it needs a trigger, though the text is vague about that). In this case the spell is not active at all until the trigger event, at which point the spell runs its course like usual.<br /> <br /> The second is an ongoing Bullet Time spell that only turns its effects on when certain conditions are met and turns them off at other times. This would be a standard Time 3 Bullet Time spell with an Entropy 2 trigger. The spell is not suspended at all, it is active but it isn't doing anything until the conditions are met. Similar to how a mage might give himself flight but not use it for every second of the spell.<br /> <br /> You are talking about the second one, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T09:32:28-08:00","id":1546803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546801#post1546801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make sure I understand you correctly:<br /> <br /> There are two ways I could see constructing a Bullet Time spell that turns on when someone shoots at you. The obvious one from looking at the rules is a Bullet Time spell put in suspended animation with an event trigger. This would be Time 4 for Trigger Effect (plus Entropy 2 if it needs a trigger, though the text is vague about that). In this case the spell is not active at all until the trigger event, at which point the spell runs its course like usual.<br /> <br /> The second is an ongoing Bullet Time spell that only turns its effects on when certain conditions are met and turns them off at other times. This would be a standard Time 3 Bullet Time spell with an Entropy 2 trigger. The spell is not suspended at all, it is active but it isn't doing anything until the conditions are met. Similar to how a mage might give himself flight but not use it for every second of the spell.<br /> <br /> You are talking about the second one, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The second one, yes.<br /> <br /> And that's why I say that adding Time 4 is useless. You don't really need to make the spell being &quot;suspended&quot; (aka not active at all until the trigger is set), if you can just make the spell be &quot;on&quot; but &quot;inactive&quot; or better saying &quot;non-functional&quot; by using Entropy 2 alone to set it to become &quot;functional&quot; when the trigger is met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T09:42:12-08:00","id":1546804,"title":"","content":"Addendum: the only way that I envision triggers being held up with Time 4 in addition to Entropy 2, is if these triggers held in &quot;time stasis&quot; do not count towards multiple effects difficult increase (since the effect is, in theory, not &quot;on&quot; while being held in suspension). In that case yes, it would be useful. VERY useful, because if that were the case, then you could just simply keep THOUSANDS of triggers upon yourself (or upon your Lab or upon your &quot;test subjects&quot;) without encumbering your magical abilities.<br /> <br /> But I don't remember anything said in that regard in any edition, but I'm not entirely sure about that, it may very well be the case and I just glossed over that fact, but this would be a powerful option to have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T11:32:16-08:00","id":1546810,"title":"","content":"Well, it is in M20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20, pg 529, &quot;How Many Effects Can I Use at Once?&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an overall note, an Effect that has a Time-based trigger, one which has been locked into another Pattern, or one that has been cast but whose duration has not yet expired, does not count toward that total.</div> </div> </div> </div>So indeed, Time Triggers don't count towards the multiple effects count. However, neither do effects with a duration, so it already wasn't a problem.<br /> <br /> That said, Time 4 can also suspend spells with instantaneous durations and that is still quite useful. Indeed one of the classic uses of a Time Trigger is to use ritual casting to prepare a powerful battle spell and keep it suspended until needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T12:38:00-08:00","id":1546813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546810#post1546810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is in M20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So indeed, Time Triggers don't count towards the multiple effects count. However, neither do effects with a duration, so it already wasn't a problem.<br /> <br /> That said, Time 4 can also suspend spells with instantaneous durations and that is still quite useful. Indeed one of the classic uses of a Time Trigger is to use ritual casting to prepare a powerful battle spell and keep it suspended until needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then, in that case I do indeed revert back to the RAW then, it is indeed useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">or one that has been cast but whose duration has not yet expired, does not count toward that total.</div> </div> </div> </div>That however seems a bit problematic. I don't remember anything of the sort from previous editions. And I'm not sure what it means. Because, if I'm reading this correctly, than there's no longer increased dif for multiple effects... Because that only makes sense if you are walking with tons of effects simultaneous, since you can only cast one per turn... And how many can you realistic cast in a single scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T13:01:31-08:00","id":1546814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546813#post1546813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That however seems a bit problematic. I don't remember anything of the sort from previous editions. And I'm not sure what it means. Because, if I'm reading this correctly, than there's no longer increased dif for multiple effects... Because that only makes sense if you are walking with tons of effects simultaneous, since you can only cast one per turn... And how many can you realistic cast in a single scene?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it seems to read in M20 is that only effects with a duration of Concentration count against the limit. The problem is, Concentration is not listed as one of the potential options for Duration. This seems like one of those things that is a holdover from an early draft that slipped by the editing process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T14:37:01-08:00","id":1546816,"title":"","content":"It's not terribly different from Revised's section on the same topic (though Time-Triggers aren't discussed there in Revised). Concentration has been part of magic in Mage, but always vague and ST-call based in what it actually means for when the increased difficulties will hit or not. &quot;Concentration&quot; isn't a category of duration in M20 (or previous editions); as in the effect ends when your concentration breaks.<br /> <br /> Rather, if a Forces mage is actively controlling fire to create a show of flame-sculptures, it's a single spell with whatever duration you got on your roll, that requires concentration. A break in your mage's concentration will cause your current fire-art to lose cohesion, but as long as you have duration left, you can have your mage recreate it by focusing again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T15:09:37-08:00","id":1546817,"title":"","content":"I would personally claim that trigger effects are too good for a 2 dot sphere. I placed conditioning on Entropy 3 in my homebrewed spheres. Time 4 is a good although slightly illogical pick that makes more sense balance wise since time needs more love.<br /> <br /> I dont buy the &quot;the spell fails till trigger&quot;. It makes no sense to me therefore i operate on the asumption that the spell is like a program with an when, for or if loop on certain elements of its effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T15:13:25-08:00","id":1546818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546816#post1546816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not terribly different from Revised's section on the same topic (though Time-Triggers aren't discussed there in Revised). Concentration has been part of magic in Mage, but always vague and ST-call based in what it actually means for when the increased difficulties will hit or not. &quot;Concentration&quot; isn't a category of duration in M20 (or previous editions); as in the effect ends when your concentration breaks.<br /> <br /> Rather, if a Forces mage is actively controlling fire to create a show of flame-sculptures, it's a single spell with whatever duration you got on your roll, that requires concentration. A break in your mage's concentration will cause your current fire-art to lose cohesion, but as long as you have duration left, you can have your mage recreate it by focusing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah never really liked duration= successes.<br /> The way we play is that effects last as long as the mage is willing to keep them up (cant keep them up while asleep) unless permament. There is a limit on how many effects a mage can concentrate on and each increases the difficulty of further magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T17:06:44-08:00","id":1546819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546817#post1546817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally claim that trigger effects are too good for a 2 dot sphere. I placed conditioning on Entropy 3 in my homebrewed spheres. Time 4 is a good although slightly illogical pick that makes more sense balance wise since time needs more love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely abhor the notion of setting effects based on &quot;I feel that...&quot;<br /> <br /> This approach of &quot;going on feelings&quot; is what have caused the innumerable examples of poorly designed effects that have infected Mage ever since the first edition, rather than analytical adherence to what each lvl is supposed to do.<br /> <br /> What Entropy 2 does is exactly to deal with conditions; Entropy 3 deals with probabilities of the matter and Entropy 4 deals with probabilities of life patterns; the &quot;I feel is too little&quot; is a poor argument to me, and simply turns the lvls of Spheres completely meaningless, thus turning all effects arbitrary which causes the exact problem I mentioned of infecting the game with nonsensical poorly designed official effects, which culminated in the abomination that is HDYDT.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bI wouldn't mind if the requirement were Entropy 4 or Forces 5 and Spirit 4 and Prime 3, if any of those were coherent with what they do, but such isn't the case. Likewise, there are things that may &quot;feel too much&quot; - as in, require too high lvls for seemingly &quot;simple tasks&quot; but alas, the system must show some coherence, otherwise we should just tell STs &quot;just go with your guts&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont buy the &quot;the spell fails till trigger&quot;. It makes no sense to me therefore i operate on the asumption that the spell is like a program with an when, for or if loop on certain elements of its effect. </div> </div> </div>But &quot;the spell fails till trigger&quot; is exactly what a trigger is. Indeed, if we are talking about computational algorithms, that's exactly what a conditional do - if executes a command or don't execute a command unless a set condition is met. &quot;If Else, Or Else, If Not&quot;, all of those are conditions that causes the algorithm to &quot;fail&quot; in a sense, unless said condition is met.<br /> <br /> The Time 4 variant (which still needs Entropy 2 on top of it mind you), is just the same but in reverse, the spell is only activate unless pre established condition is met. So instead of &quot;fails till trigger&quot; is &quot;only activates when trigger&quot;, but is essentially the same concept, so I don't see why you would be against the concept if that's the exact idea of &quot;triggers&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T17:37:21-08:00","id":1546820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546816#post1546816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not terribly different from Revised's section on the same topic (though Time-Triggers aren't discussed there in Revised). Concentration has been part of magic in Mage, but always vague and ST-call based in what it actually means for when the increased difficulties will hit or not. &quot;Concentration&quot; isn't a category of duration in M20 (or previous editions); as in the effect ends when your concentration breaks.<br /> <br /> Rather, if a Forces mage is actively controlling fire to create a show of flame-sculptures, it's a single spell with whatever duration you got on your roll, that requires concentration. A break in your mage's concentration will cause your current fire-art to lose cohesion, but as long as you have duration left, you can have your mage recreate it by focusing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that realistically, it's next to impossible to &quot;concentrate&quot; on multiple effects - imagine trying to make flames dance at your will with Forces 2 while at the same time sculpting a three with Life 2 and simultaneously shaping clay into a statue with Matter 3 and all that while you're reading somebody's mind at the same time... That seems absolutely impossible.<br /> <br /> &quot;Concentration&quot; after all, implies focusing on a single task... If you are multitasking, you are NOT concentrate...<br /> <br /> Unless you use Mind 1 to be able to fully focus on each one of these tasks as if your entire attention were set on each individual one, upon which such dif penalties then should just simply disappear. I still think there's something missing here, like Ramnesis said, this appear to be the leftovers of some earlier draft that got half baked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-09T20:10:47-08:00","id":1546827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546816#post1546816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not terribly different from Revised's section on the same topic (though Time-Triggers aren't discussed there in Revised). Concentration has been part of magic in Mage, but always vague and ST-call based in what it actually means for when the increased difficulties will hit or not. &quot;Concentration&quot; isn't a category of duration in M20 (or previous editions); as in the effect ends when your concentration breaks.<br /> <br /> Rather, if a Forces mage is actively controlling fire to create a show of flame-sculptures, it's a single spell with whatever duration you got on your roll, that requires concentration. A break in your mage's concentration will cause your current fire-art to lose cohesion, but as long as you have duration left, you can have your mage recreate it by focusing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, which is why I only recently picked up on its absence in M20. It\u2019s easy to assume it is there, but the only reference to it is in the section that renders it mostly irrelevant. Hence why I think it is at least partially an editing mixup.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T00:19:19-08:00","id":1546829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546819#post1546819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Time 4 variant (which still needs Entropy 2 on top of it mind you), is just the same but in reverse, the spell is only activate unless pre established condition is met. So instead of &quot;fails till trigger&quot; is &quot;only activates when trigger&quot;, but is essentially the same concept, so I don't see why you would be against the concept if that's the exact idea of &quot;triggers&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what im saying , the reverse as you said with time 4 makes sense, the continiously failing does not.<br /> <br /> I would not say Entropy 2 deals with conditions. Its more like setting the outcome of ongoing nonliving processes. Here i have to say that Entropy does not affect magic (yuo cant make casting a spell easier or in consequence cant trigger a magical effect). If it could it shouldbe specifically stated so like it is in the time sphere.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;I feel that&quot; its not a bad way of doing things if you have homebrewed the sphere lvls from scratch. Example how my Entropy looks:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0 Detection of probability, finding weaknesses, decay detection.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Influence on the outcome of uncomplicated probability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Creation of probable uncomplicated probability, event trigger.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Healing, decay, blessings/curses (luck), influence on complex probability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Creation of destiny, creation of complex probability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">^ Uncomplicated probability does not affect the fate or decision-making of sentient beings.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T06:59:41-08:00","id":1546834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546829#post1546829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats what im saying , the reverse as you said with time 4 makes sense, the continiously failing does not.<br /> <br /> I would not say Entropy 2 deals with conditions. Its more like setting the outcome of ongoing nonliving processes. Here i have to say that Entropy does not affect magic (yuo cant make casting a spell easier or in consequence cant trigger a magical effect). If it could it shouldbe specifically stated so like it is in the time sphere.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;I feel that&quot; its not a bad way of doing things if you have homebrewed the sphere lvls from scratch. Example how my Entropy looks:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Entropy</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0 Detection of probability, finding weaknesses, decay detection.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Influence on the outcome of uncomplicated probability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Creation of probable uncomplicated probability, event trigger.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Healing, decay, blessings/curses (luck), influence on complex probability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0\ud804\uddd0 Creation of destiny, creation of complex probability.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">^ Uncomplicated probability does not affect the fate or decision-making of sentient beings.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine to homebrew the Spheres, I do it myself, but then you need to get internal consistency with what you make, which is so many times not the case on official effects. I'm also a GURPS player, and I usually say that WoD was created by artists while GURPS was created by engineers. It seems that when writing WoD, the writers just had uncontrollable explosions of Glamour; the system is absolutely amazing and beautiful, a real work of art, but it so often lacks consistency because it has too much Glamour but not enough &quot;good Banality&quot; to keep it grounded, and MtA is possibly the worst offender, because they've created the best Magic system of all time at the time (and it's still one of the best that exist), but got all embroiled when it was time to apply it in a coherent way - too much Glamour, not enough Banality. Meanwhile, GURPS is so stiff and rigid, it is the most grounded system, but it needs to relax a little bit sometimes. I like to mix the two, and I play a GURPS-WoD which fits to my tastes.<br /> <br /> Entropy 2 can affect magic thou, it can reduce difficulty. But it's an extra step, you would have to cast it as a further effect; usually it's not worth it. But it functions similarly to &quot;abilities helping magic&quot;. But it definitely can help. You could use it in your Sanctum, but you'll probably already have several arrangements there to reduce dif as much as possible, so it would just be redundant, and in the field (aka in the middle of a bar fight) it's simply not worth to waste an entire turn so that the spell you'll only cast at the next turn will be a bit easier. But it is technically doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T07:45:47-08:00","id":1546836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546834#post1546834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entropy 2 can affect magic thou, it can reduce difficulty. But it's an extra step, you would have to cast it as a further effect; usually it's not worth it. But it functions similarly to &quot;abilities helping magic&quot;. But it definitely can help. You could use it in your Sanctum, but you'll probably already have several arrangements there to reduce dif as much as possible, so it would just be redundant, and in the field (aka in the middle of a bar fight) it's simply not worth to waste an entire turn so that the spell you'll only cast at the next turn will be a bit easier. But it is technically doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Show me where it says it can. If it could it could be completely broken as you could just make it an prelonged buff for lets say a day and cast all spells that day with even -6 (3 from tools 3 from entropy)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T08:08:48-08:00","id":1546837,"title":"","content":"What is Entropy actually doing to suspend a spell, though? Acting as a trigger I understand, but actually suspending the spell and keeping it around until a certain point doesn't make sense with this sphere. What's the mechanism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T10:30:14-08:00","id":1546844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546837#post1546837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is Entropy actually doing to suspend a spell, though? Acting as a trigger I understand, but actually suspending the spell and keeping it around until a certain point doesn't make sense with this sphere. What's the mechanism?</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not have to suspend a spell. I see it more like the spell is active just the doing thing part is off and gets on with a switch if the requirements are met.<br /> Suspending something is more of a time thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T11:11:02-08:00","id":1546847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546844#post1546844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does not have to suspend a spell. I see it more like the spell is active just the doing thing part is off and gets on with a switch if the requirements are met.<br /> Suspending something is more of a time thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that leaves two elements, the sphere(s) to set the conditions for turning off and on, and the sphere to turn off and on.<br /> <br /> For the latter... overall I don't think there's a need for a sphere to do that. There's nothing written about it that I am aware of. Consciously controlled spells don't need that. For instance, someone with a flight spell can probably still walk normally if they want to. Ward and Time Trigger, likewise, have nothing about needing an activation/deactivation sphere even when they are clearly changing behavior in response to something. <br /> <br /> That being said, if there did need to be such a sphere, Entropy would be the best candidate, and Entropy 3 is the most fitting rank based on description. It's a shaky fit, though.<br /> <br /> As for letting a spell detect conditions, I'm firmly of the opinion that should be Entropy 2 (or other relevant sphere at 2). It's essentially a perception effect, but added to the spell instead of the mage, so I push it one rank higher for the alternate use but never higher. Perception effects don't take higher ranks the more complicated the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-10T13:15:42-08:00","id":1546849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546847#post1546847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that leaves two elements, the sphere(s) to set the conditions for turning off and on, and the sphere to turn off and on.<br /> <br /> For the latter... overall I don't think there's a need for a sphere to do that. There's nothing written about it that I am aware of. Consciously controlled spells don't need that. For instance, someone with a flight spell can probably still walk normally if they want to. Ward and Time Trigger, likewise, have nothing about needing an activation/deactivation sphere even when they are clearly changing behavior in response to something.<br /> <br /> That being said, if there did need to be such a sphere, Entropy would be the best candidate, and Entropy 3 is the most fitting rank based on description. It's a shaky fit, though.<br /> <br /> As for letting a spell detect conditions, I'm firmly of the opinion that should be Entropy 2 (or other relevant sphere at 2). It's essentially a perception effect, but added to the spell instead of the mage, so I push it one rank higher for the alternate use but never higher. Perception effects don't take higher ranks the more complicated the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not call the example given as deactivation. When you stop levitating you still use your levitation control to walk unless you want to break the spell. I dont think you can deactivate a spell and activate it again on your own. Thats why i use Entropy 3 for it.<br /> <br /> Still i feel time should be able to do more things. Not sure what though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-05T08:51:44-08:00","id":1547546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steve Bridger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1546723-do-while-and-do-until-spell-contingencies?p=1546733#post1546733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the caveat that this is largely guesswork and interpretation on my part, since it's not spelled out anywhere I can locate, Entropy <i>seems</i> to work conjunctionally to create &quot;conditions&quot; in other effects by deliberately creating a sort of &quot;loose thread&quot; in the weave of an overall working, and ties that to some other potential condition in the tapestry, deterministically linking the two. I can imagine an Etherite describing this as some sort of &quot;causal ethric entanglement.&quot; The mage who's trying to do this thinks of this application of Entropy as coding conditions (if-then, do-while, do-until, etc.) and function breaks. The player actually works out his rotes in the form of pseudocode on paper, he's that much into the &quot;reality hacking&quot; business.<br /> <br /> In the case of hanging effects with conditions, the &quot;loose thread&quot; is the Time aspect. When some other specified condition causes it to be pulled, that undoes the temporal statis the rest of the working has been locked into.<br /> <br /> The most complete explanation in the written material I can find requires different levels of Entropy, depending on what you're wanting to link an effect to conditionally. The levels seem to be based on what sorts of things Entropy itself can work with in a probabilistic sense. (I am not totally clear on what counts as &quot;ideas,&quot; requiring Entropy 5, except maybe a condition based on some person or group of people merely thinking of something?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a very controversial and complicated subject, since Mage never explained or provided rules for suspending spells and etc. I had a thread with a similar idea, where we discussed what were the advantages of Time 4, if a mage could just &quot;turn on/off&quot; spells without it. You can look it up on search tool. I started it and I think the title is Time 4, or something.<br /> <br /> Back to your thread, no Entropy does not trigger nor affects spellcasting. It affects probability/decay. The reason people always want to use Entropy is because, for some reason, Entropy 2 was used in Time 4 triggers. In my opinion, that's sphere bloat. All you need for a Time 4 trigger is Time 4 (if your trigger is related to time, i.e.: cast the spell 3 hours later) or another sphere, related to your trigger.<br /> <br /> So, if you want a spell to be cast when you are hurt, you need Time and Life. Life will tell when you are hurt. I would say the same applies to your &quot;always running&quot; spell. You want a lightbulb to light when someone enters. Entripy had nothing to do with electricity nor people. You need Forces +Prime to power the lightbulb and Life to detect that someone has entered the place. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}